+# Old preemption development checkpoint
+
+Baseline: OpenJDK 25u `1fac148c2dcc5c2f065999ff3562a76e3c699d0f`.
+This is an experimental implementation requiring the validation described below.
+The previous transient environment was lost. Recovered commits form a new history;
+the earlier HotSpot startup observation does not validate this reconstruction.
+
+## Protocol and changes
+
+| Files under `src/hotspot/share/gc/z/` | Purpose |
+| --- | --- |
+| `zOldPreemption.hpp`, `.cpp` | Old-local condition-variable participation, stack-preserving park/resume, cycle/epoch/progress logs |
+| `zDriver.cpp` | Request before acquiring the shared driver lock; release the hold after Minor and driver unlock |
+| `zTask.hpp`, `.cpp`, `zWorkers.hpp`, `.cpp` | Classify audited tasks; transfer participation from waiting driver to active Old workers |
+| `zMark.cpp`, `zMarkTerminate.inline.hpp` | Poll between mark entries; publish both generations' local stacks; leave participation around termination waits |
+| `zRelocate.hpp`, `.cpp` | Reference-count relocation holds so safepoint end cannot release the Minor hold; keep the original iterator/task/forwardings |
+| `zGeneration.cpp` | Driver phase boundaries and page checkpoints; preserve the Remap + Relocate Start transaction |
+| `zReferenceProcessor.cpp`, `zWeakRootsProcessor.cpp` | Park at existing safe STS yield sites without losing discovered-list locals |
+| `zRelocationSet.cpp` | Checkpoints at page installation/destruction boundaries |
+| `zBreakpoint.cpp` | Avoid preemption deadlocks while waiting for WhiteBox GC breakpoints |
+| `z_globals.hpp` | Diagnostic enable switch and a debug-build-only interruptible stress delay |
+
+Minor sets an Old-only request and waits for active participants to leave STS
+and park. Driver participation remains active throughout unaudited transactions.
+Audited tasks transfer participation to their workers; blocking mark termination
+and breakpoint waits release participation with RAII and reacquire it before
+continuing. Old marking publishes both generations' per-thread mark stacks before
+parking. Bitmap, stripe state, task objects and C++ local variables remain alive.
+No preemption path invokes abort or resets the Major cycle. Existing shutdown
+abort and worker resize behavior remain present.
+
+Once participants are stopped, Minor takes a relocation synchronization hold.
+The existing safepoint hold nests with it. Releasing a safepoint hold cannot wake
+the background iterator while the Minor hold remains. Minor runs and releases
+its driver lock, then releases relocation and participant holds.
+
+`-Xlog:gc+preempt=debug` records cycle, phase, request, epoch and progress snapshots,
+wait and pause durations, and Minor start/end. `gc+preempt=trace` adds worker
+park/resume events; use uptime/thread decorators when investigating latency.
+`mark_entries` counts processed stack entries, not unique marked objects;
+`relocated_pages` counts completed forwardings. These counters support diagnostics
+and cannot on their own prove heap correctness.
+
+## Boundaries and known limitations
+
+Mark follow, discovered-reference traversal, weak-root callbacks and relocation
+set installation can park in their original C++ call frames. Reset and selection
+poll between items; page-table iteration releases its safe-destroy guard first.
+
+Mark Roots, Mark Free, class unlink/purge internals, handshake/rendezvous, bulk
+selector operations and the Remap Young Roots + Relocate Start transaction remain
+serial. Their locks, CLD/nmethod lifetime, resurrection state and root/remset epoch
+invariants have not been proven safe for arbitrary-duration suspension inside
+those operations. Inter-operation checkpoints do not bound these operations.
+
+Relocate Start reserves queue workers before their tasks launch. The driver must
+run relocation setup and launch those workers before parking; otherwise a Minor
+would wait forever for reserved workers which never started.
+
+Relocation polls at page boundaries. A page/in-place transaction or hard page
+fault must finish first and may have substantial latency. **Urgent queued
+forwardings still run during a hold**: the original queue contract requires
+servicing callers which cannot enter a blocking state. Suppressing them can
+deadlock Young or mutators. Thus strict zero Old relocation during every Minor
+and the requested latency behavior under all paging/allocation-stall conditions
+are not established by this MVP. No new mutator bulk copying, pacing, priority
+changes, forced Old quantum, or full-Minor global STS synchronization was added.
+
+## Build and validate
+
+Read the checked-out `doc/building.md` and `bash configure --help` for host setup.
+Use `JDK_BOOT_HOME` (native JDK 24/25), `JTREG_HOME` (jtreg 8 image), and run
+`preemption/build-linux.sh` or, on Windows with Cygwin/MSYS2 plus Visual Studio
+2022 and Windows SDK, `preemption/build-windows.sh`. Extra arguments pass through
+to configure. `DEBUG_LEVEL=release` selects a release image after fastdebug tests.
+The Windows script has not itself produced a Windows JDK in this Linux host.
+
+There is no `hotspot_gc_z` group in this baseline. Use
+`make CONF=<conf> test TEST=test/hotspot/jtreg/gc/z` with
+`JTREG='JOBS=2;TIMEOUT_FACTOR=3;JAVA_OPTIONS=-XX:+UseZGC'`.
+First run `TEST=test/hotspot/jtreg/gc/z/TestOldPreemption.java`, then the whole
+directory, `gc/stress/gcold/TestGCOldWithZ.java` and
+`gc/stress/gcbasher/TestGCBasherWithZ.java`. Preserve `.jtr`, GC logs and crash files.
+
+The new stress test slows only Old safe polls using an interruptible monitor
+wait in fastdebug, keeps a young allocation/old-to-young pointer workload running,
+checks strong/weak/phantom references and reclamation, and requires completion of
+the same Major after at least 32 holds with monotonic progress. It requires
+observed Mark, reference-processing and relocation interruptions. This test is
+not a replacement for paging, class unloading, allocation-stall or in-place
+relocation tests, nor is a 32-pause run evidence of hundreds of pauses per cycle.
+
+`LatencyProbe.java` uses only upstream WhiteBox calls for a same-workload baseline
+comparison. Compile it with `test/lib/jdk/test/whitebox/WhiteBox.java` and its
+parser dependencies, then run each JDK with `-XX:+UseZGC -Xms256m -Xmx512m
+-XX:+UnlockDiagnosticVMOptions -XX:+WhiteBoxAPI -Xbootclasspath/a:<classes>
+-cp <classes> -Xlog:gc*:file=<log> LatencyProbe`.
+The reported Minor wall time includes request delivery and any preemption wait.
+Record Allocation Stall log counts separately. A warm resident-heap comparison
+does not establish behavior with the user's externally imposed priorities and
+swapped-out Old pages.
+
+Final test/build evidence and delivery locations are recorded in `RESULTS.md`.
